  "procedure": {
    "application": "Signed, debuggable embedded apps, with separate ordinary build profiles for Android WebView and each embedded V8. Native replay uses the WebView-profile APK and launches no WebView script process.",
    "bytes": "Counts refer to the packed command payload received by the app. The three live hosts captured byte-identical frames; native replay reads those packets from its local tape. Per-frame counts exclude method arguments, VM/IPC bookkeeping, signing and initial atlas uploads. No physical Binder byte count was measured.",
    "pixels": "Independent CPU barycentric triangle coverage, nearest atlas lookup, rectangular clipping and authored paint order at the terminal pose (logical frame 209). An interior pixel is one whose 3×3 expected neighborhood has uniform color. Exact comparisons retain both full-image differences and interior pixels; all colors are opaque. Categorization identifies neighboring CPU-reference colors and layers, without assigning a driver cause.",
    "lifecycle": "After the terminal frame, Home backgrounds the Activity. Resuming creates a second EGL context, uploads both pages again and redraws the terminal frame. Closing the embedded game records four texture-page releases in total and zero renderer abandon calls. The script or tape close receipt is separate. Individual driver allocations were not measured.",
    "timing": "Four process-cold launches per lane in a balanced four-by-four order. Each run submits 210 frames, excludes the first 30 callbacks, and samples 180 successive real UI-thread submission-callback intervals. Each process uses a nearest-rank p95. Summary p95 is the median of the four process p95s. Pixel checks, dumpsys and memory sampling occur outside the 180-frame window. The deterministic animation advances at 120 logical steps per second. The interval is neither GPU execution duration nor a display presentation timestamp."
  },
